-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "542c6e90-f80c-52ae-9fc3-bff7b0448653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec{\\left(2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "542c6e90-f80c-52ae-9fc3-bff7b0448653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec{\\left(2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677406} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe29454b-a75b-5c7f-a6bf-aeaa639f5f41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677456}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ad177de-f56b-548a-80fb-4041da0c0739" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\tan{\\left(2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 \\tan{\\left(2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sec{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\sec{\\left(2 x - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70f50210-11fa-5e51-88d9-cb55ccf10758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5} - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70f50210-11fa-5e51-88d9-cb55ccf10758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5} - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref