ifficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a973650d-44b5-5568-9c49-20e47dc4a2f2" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}} 4 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 3 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=- \\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=- \\frac{\\pi}{12}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed bounds decrease; keep their order when subtracting endpoint values.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{12}} 4 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- 3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{4 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}=\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b991a52b-4050-5c87-98f1-935ba7acf9ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{9 \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b991a52b-4050-5c87-98f1-935ba7acf9ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{9 \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677432} :answer-field/id #uuid "90a82afe-9b5c-5581-ac29-11654aefd369" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677422}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ae5adf82-5498-5c01-a1b8-4a2da93e2ba3" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}} - \\frac{3 \\sec^{2}{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}} - \\frac{3 \\sec^{2}{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{9}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{9 \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}=\\left(- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{9}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{9 \\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677434 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a89b39e9-4843-5bc6-87aa-fddaf1966f77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a89b39e9-4843-5bc6-87aa-fddaf1966f77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677429} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e566b4b-c7af-511a-99be-fd1ad29079da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677419}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bf265989-f6f0-5f0e-ba70-db7eef3eab20" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{5 \\pi}{6}}^{\\pi} - \\frac{2 \\csc^{2}{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{5 \\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\\\x=\\pi&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{5 \\pi}{6}}^{\\pi} - \\frac{2 \\csc^{2}{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{4 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}=\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee967d5-fefd-5922-921c-94cee5140c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ee967d5-fefd-5922-921c-94cee5140c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677420} :answer-field/id #uuid "23e14db0-4119-5331-8607-daa0c44fb68d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677395}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c583b2c4-8e86-5ae3-86a7-7860d0969586" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{15}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{10}} \\cot{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(5 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=5 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{15}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{10}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{15}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{10}} \\cot{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(5 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{5}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[- \\frac{\\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{5}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}=\\left(- \\frac{1}{5}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{15}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{15}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677438 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b0aa95c-2405-5271-89be-bd02c6d33269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{6} + \\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b0aa95c-2405-5271-89be-bd02c6d33269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{6} + \\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677401} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f481514-f665-5049-865b-c270ae2e8eaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677426}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5b1ad32-bb4e-5508-bddb-594979f05fa7" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{24}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{18}} - 7 \\csc^{2}{\\left(6 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=6 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=6.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{24}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{18}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{24}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{18}} - 7 \\csc^{2}{\\left(6 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{7}{6}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{7 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}}{6}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}=\\left(\\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{18}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{7}{6}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n- \\frac{7}{6} + \\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{18}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677443 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "863b5b27-ae04-5906-aacf-0d5ac60e3a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\csc{\\left(- 2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "863b5b27-ae04-5906-aacf-0d5ac60e3a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\csc{\\left(- 2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677417} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f8104c5-b0a2-5cfc-b3e1-6a64e97e59f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677421}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e415d708-3e73-5f13-95d7-e0704f439fd7" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 5 \\cot{\\left(- 2 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- 2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 5 \\cot{\\left(- 2 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- 2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{5}{2}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{5}{2}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{5 \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5 \\csc{\\left(- 2 x \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677449 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7a5d38e-3a33-59bc-991f-be6ec110bb4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{15}{4} + \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7a5d38e-3a33-59bc-991f-be6ec110bb4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{15}{4} + \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677453} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef41ae03-0363-5ab5-8c19-b5a72d57172d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677450}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ebd5575e-4739-5634-aaed-010e3b1faf38" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} - \\frac{5 \\sec^{2}{\\left(- \\frac{2 x}{3} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- \\frac{2 x}{3} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed bounds decrease; keep their order when subtracting endpoint values.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} - \\frac{5 \\sec^{2}{\\left(- \\frac{2 x}{3} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{15}{4}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and evaluate at both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{15 \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}=\\left(\\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{15}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nSimplifying gives\n\n$$\n- \\frac{15}{4} + \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677454 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d79d7341-1973-5d7b-ac0b-0797293dbe4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7 \\sec{\\left(- 5 x \\right)}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d79d7341-1973-5d7b-ac0b-0797293dbe4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7 \\sec{\\left(- 5 x \\right)}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677439} :answer-field/id #uuid "00f7e62b-077a-54d7-8638-cd1efc363493" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677386}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9a8cd21-dc7c-5e67-8cfe-457222aa02c9" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 7 \\tan{\\left(- 5 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(- 5 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 5 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-5.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 7 \\tan{\\left(- 5 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(- 5 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{7}{5}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{7}{5}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{7 \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}}{5}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{7 \\sec{\\left(- 5 x \\right)}}{5}+C.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions With Linear Arguments"}]}
